findings:
Attitude round trip (stick to the body rate seen in mocap):
- rig bag 17-24 ms (h2, h2rts, h2slope, f2slope, h3; R² 0.6-0.86; stable across 1-15 Hz bands);
- rig log 27-36 ms;
- twin base from the 60 ms runs (R2381/84/85/88, pitch R² 0.93-0.98): 109-117 ms minus 60 = 49-57 ms.
The twin's emulated rate PID (kp 0.5, ki 5) is slower than Betaflight.

Loop phases at f0:
- throttle lag behind -dz': rig ema 41-75 ms, rig slope 23-26 ms, twin delayed 57-102 ms;
- reference trail along z: rig 62-95 ms (h2rts 20 ms, and it still swung), twin 55-72 ms;
- along the line: rig 93-116 ms, twin 52-72 ms, ref/act 1.24-1.58 on both.
The reference minus position lags the position by 86-111 deg, so the planner's trail acts as damping, not as the pump.

Thrust power at f0, taking the throttle 20-70 ms late:
- vertical damps on every rig flight (c_z +1.7 to +6.9 N s/m), more with slope;
- along-line feeds the swing with ema (c_u -0.14 to -1.20 on h2, h2t9p, h2rts, c2q) and damps it with slope (-0.05 to +1.38 on h2slope, f2slope);
- twin cd060/cd080: c_u +1.1 to +2.6, c_z about +0.5 to +0.9 at the delay assumed.
The energy does not balance, so treat these as phases.

Ruled out or weakened:
- the vertical reference trail (h2rts);
- the measured-pull loop (h2m, planned pull, swung 4.22 deg);
- the ring's velocity on slope (R2380: 6.09 against 5.6 deg);
- the uniform Smith predictor (R2375-R2378: at most a 10-20 % cut);
- elastic cables;
- ROS, ELRS and planner timing.
